<p>Iran’s foreign minister, Abbas Araghchi, says a nuclear agreement with the United States is “within reach” ahead of talks scheduled for Thursday in Geneva. He cast the moment as a chance to address “mutual concerns” — if “diplomacy is given priority”. A senior U.S. official said the talks will take place Thursday in Geneva. The push comes as the U.S. raises its military posture in the Middle East, a buildup described as meant to increase pressure on Tehran. The White House says President Donald Trump prefers to try diplomacy first, but is prepared to use force if necessary.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/TAQyRVyh2xDNRn4uFOd6mt5kZO5AT4CE4GUvJzZYtMRVd71cLlDdYHOhMCcYyU6W77UJI8pZaVCIbxznvAXCXEONBUbdn6zga1MXGyMxmJIn' alt='Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi speaks to the media at UN headquarters in New York City (file photo, Sept. 25, 2024).' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Who’s negotiating: U.S. envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner are slated to meet an Iranian delegation in Geneva.</li><li>Iran’s message: Deputy Foreign Minister Majid Takht-Ravanchi said Iran wants an agreement “as soon as possible,” will do “whatever it takes,” and will negotiate “with complete honesty and good faith”.</li><li>Iran’s warning: Tehran has threatened to strike U.S. bases in the region if it is attacked.</li><li>At home: Al-Monitor reported that the government issued a muted warning toward student protesters as external pressure and nuclear talks continued.</li></ul><blockquote>We have a historic opportunity to strike an unprecedented agreement that addresses mutual concerns and achieves mutual interests - Abbas Araghchi</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi: In a post on X, he said a deal is “within reach,” but only if “diplomacy is given priority,” calling it a chance for an agreement that serves mutual interests. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/25/irans-fm-says-deal-with-us-within-reach-if-diplomacy-given-priority'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>White House (Press Secretary Karoline Leavitt): She said President Trump’s first option is diplomacy, while also saying he is willing to use lethal force if needed. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1975497/iran-fm-says-nuclear-deal-within-reach-ahead-of-us-talks'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Iranian Deputy Foreign Minister Majid Takht-Ravanchi: He said Iran is ready to reach an agreement “as soon as possible,” would do “whatever it takes,” and would enter the negotiating room “with complete honesty and good faith.” (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/iran-ready-any-necessary-steps-reach-deal-us-deputy-foreign-minister-says'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-iran-us-nuclear-talks-geneva/'>Iran’s foreign minister says U.S. deal is close, but only if ‘diplomacy is given priority’</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1975497/iran-fm-says-nuclear-deal-within-reach-ahead-of-us-talks'>Iran FM says nuclear deal ‘within reach’ ahead of US talks</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/02/24/iran-says-an-unprecedented-deal-is-within-reach-ahead-of-us-talks_6750844_4.html'>Iran says &#x27;unprecedented&#x27; deal &#x27;within reach&#x27; ahead of US talks</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-fm-says-nuclear-deal-within-reach-ahead-of-us-talks/article70672892.ece'>Iran FM says nuclear deal &#x27;within reach&#x27; ahead of U.S. talks</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/iran-ready-any-necessary-steps-reach-deal-us-deputy-foreign-minister-says'>Iran is ready for any necessary steps to reach deal with US, deputy foreign minister says</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/25/irans-fm-says-deal-with-us-within-reach-if-diplomacy-given-priority'>Iran’s FM says deal wit